  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "An equilateral triangle has the same perimeter as a regular decagon whose side is $6\\,mm.$ Find the length of the side of the triangle.",
  "worked_solution": "Since all the sides of the decagon are equal, its perimeter is\n\n$$\np=10\\cdot 6=60\\,mm.\n$$\n\nLet $a$ be the side of the equilateral triangle. We know that our polygons have equal perimeters. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =3a \\\\ 60 & =3a \\\\ 20 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the side is $20\\,mm.$",
